/* book Worked example 2: Q: Compare the moment a beam 230 mm wide with an effective depth of 450 mm (M20, Fe415) may carry at service load by the working stress method and by the limit state method, designed as a balanced singly reinforced section in each method. For the limit state method take Mu,lim = 0.138 fck b d² and γf = 1.5.
   1. WSM: Q = 0.913 N/mm² (see working stress method). MR = Q b d² = 0.913 × 230 × 450² = 42.5 kNm, at service load.
   2. LSM: Mu,lim = 0.138 × 20 × 230 × 450² = 128.5 kNm, at factored load.
   3. Service moment allowed by LSM = 128.5/1.5 = 85.7 kNm.
   4. Ratio 85.7/42.5 = 2.0: the same concrete section carries about twice the service moment by limit state design, because it uses the material strength beyond the elastic range. It needs more steel to do so, and its deflection and cracking must then be checked.
   Answer: WSM allows 42.5 kNm at service; LSM allows 128.5/1.5 = 85.7 kNm, about twice as much, subject to the serviceability checks. */
